{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Region Event Routing.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Region Event Routing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender region event routing blender region event routing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Region Event Routing.md","fileName":"Blender Region Event Routing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Region Event Routing","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Operator and Event System]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Screen Area Structure","Blender Region Structure","Blender Event Handler Structure","Blender Operator Handler Dispatch","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Region Event Routing.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Region Event Routing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender region event routing blender region event routing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Region Event Routing.md","fileName":"Blender Region Event Routing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Region Event Routing","heading":"Blender Region Event Routing","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Region event routing determines which part of the active Blender screen should receive an event. The dispatcher first checks a [[Blender Screen Area Structure]] boundary, then searches its [[Blender Region Structure]] list and sets the matching area and region in context.\n\nThis spatial test combines with mode and state checks rather than replacing them. Once the location is known, the event and that region's [[Blender Event Handler Structure]] list pass to [[Blender Operator Handler Dispatch]], where polling can decide whether a candidate operation is valid.","tags":["ba